## **WHY I DID NOT SPLEEP LAST NIGHT?**

The dust has barely settled on the Monterey Peninsula, but the big money di=
dn't pack up and go home. If you spent any time watching the boards yesterd=
ay, you saw $6.63M shift hands across 26 six-figure cars online. The physic=
al auctions in California might be over, but the digital platforms are imme=
diately absorbing the unspent capital of frustrated underbidders who missed=
 out on the physical auction blocks.

Bring a Trailer completely dominated yesterday's action, taking home 25 of =
the 26 six-figure sales. Cars & Bids logged a single, high-profile closing =
with a 992-generation Porsche 911 GT3 finding a new home for $266,500. It i=
s clear that the modern GT and analog V12 market is not experiencing any po=
st-Monterey hangover; instead, we are seeing immediate, highly liquid redep=
loyment of cash.

The daily volume trajectory illustrates a steady mid-week momentum. The mar=
ket has found its late-summer rhythm, showing consistent daily turnover as =
high-end collectors seek out curated specs without the physical auction hou=
se premiums.



